<DocsPage id="composer">

          <p>
            The box at the bottom of a session is where you type the task, and it carries every per-message control: which agent answers, which model, how hard that model thinks, how fast to run, dictation, and attachments. It takes pasted images and dragged files, keeps a history of your prompts you can walk back through, and offers a popover of slash commands. Shell mode sends a command instead of a prompt, and it is refused while Plan Mode is on.
          </p>
          <h3>Model effort</h3>
          <p>
            For models that expose reasoning effort, the model popover shows a slider across that model's variants: <strong>Default</strong> follows the provider's recommendation, <strong>Light</strong> favours speed and cost on small tasks, <strong>Balanced</strong> trades speed against careful reasoning, and <strong>Max</strong> sits at the top of the range. The choice shows on the control, with its description in the tooltip.
          </p>
          <h3>Execution speed</h3>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li><strong>Normal</strong><span>Standard speed and token use.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Quick</strong><span>Answers simple questions with minimal context and fewer tokens.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Fast</strong><span>Around 1.5× the speed, with priority capacity and wider parallel execution, at a higher token cost.</span></li>
          </ul>
</DocsPage>
